10. Performance budget

Record baseline metrics before changing the scene, then compare after the course is implemented on the same available runtime/device.

Measure, where supported:

* Frame-time distribution, including P50/P95 and spikes during course traversal.
* renderer.info.render.calls, triangles, geometry count and texture count.
* Memory/resource counts across repeated scene creation and disposal.
* Cost of the active dust effect.
* Performance while viewing the entire course and while passing beneath the elevated section.

Targets:

* Aim for 60 FPS on a representative desktop/browser and at least 30 FPS on supported mobile hardware, where the runtime allows a real measurement.
* Avoid more than a 10% frame-time regression against the measured baseline on the same device.
* Aim for no more than 12 additional steady-state draw calls for the course itself, using merged geometry and instancing where practical.
* Do not claim a device target passed if you could not test on that device. Record the hardware/runtime and method used.

If a target fails, profile and fix the cause. Do not conceal regressions by lowering quality settings without measuring the trade-off.

